six months after a missing las vegas  woman was found  dead one of the men connected to her  death is now in police custody  22 year old leslie palacio was murdered  back in august  her body later discovered right near the  valley of fire state park  sasha loftis spoke with leslie's family  tonight and she joins us now live  outside of the clark county detention  center with more on their message  denise and brian jose rangel is at the  clark county detention center tonight  after  months on the run in mexico now i talked  to leslie palacio's family they say  they're relieved  but they won't truly find peace until  both men connected to her death  are behind bars  it's been six months since leslie  palacio's life was suddenly stolen  this is just the beginning of it we need  to find  the main person that killed my sister  her family hasn't given up their pain  propelling a search for the men  connected to her murder a major break in  the case  came just a few weeks ago when one of  those men jose rangel was arrested near  the u.s  mexico border it was a big relief but  you know that's just the beginning we  need to catch the main character  that main character is jose's son eric  rangalibada  the 25 year old accused of killing  leslie  police say he and jose left the country  after dumping her body near valley of  fire state park  back in september officers believe eric  remains on the run in mexico  leslie's mother is still pushing for  answers  as her entire family prays for peace she  didn't deserve  to be like this she didn't deserve it  jose's capture is a step in the right  direction  but those who loved leslie say this  isn't over  they won't rest until justice is served  we're not going to stop until he's eric  is finally caught  jose rangel faces multiple charges  tonight including aiding a felony  offender  and destroying or concealing evidence if  you have any information  as to where eric rongalibara could be  please call metro police  or crime stoppers 